title: International Relations
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: international_relations_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; international_relations_timer += 12;
card-image: img/international.jpg
max-visits: 4
#subtitle: Building ties with our fraternal socialist parties.

Through contacts abroad, we can build ties with sister liberal parties, internationalist movements, and sympathetic governments.

- @fr_uk: Build relationships with the French Parti Radicale and British Liberal Party to move their governments in Germany's favor.
- @austria: Push the Austrian public towards German unification through liberal contacts.
- @paneuropa: Support Coudenhove-Kalergi's Pan-European movement.
- @dutch_scandi: Learn how to survive as a small liberal party from the Dutch VDB and the scandinavian Liberal parties.
- @league_of_nations: Support League of Nations membership for Germany.
- @america: Talk to our contacts in america amongst the Democratic and Republican Party.
- @return: We do not need international contacts at the moment.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@fr_uk
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; west_relation += 1; linksliberale_strength += 3; reparations_negotiation += 1

The British Liberals and the French Radical Party are the closest thing we have to sister parties abroad. Their influence, even diminished, can be used to bear in favor of easing our reparations burden and rebuilding trust between our countries.

@austria
subtitle: -1 resources [? if austrian_parliament_seen and not austrian_civil_war_seen: - We will also help the Austrians oppose their dictatorship. ?]
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
audio: shuffle music/communist/workers_of_vienna_normalized.mp3
on-arrival: resources -= 1; nationalliberale_strength += 3; nationalism += 1*(1-dissent); east_relation -= 1; austria_unification_opinion += 1

The Treaty forbids it, but we do not believe the principle of national self-determination should stop at Austria's border. We should therefore gain goodwill amongst the austrian people and goverment and work towards unification.

@dutch_scandi
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; sammlung_strength += 5; sammlung_dissent -= 5 if sammlung_dissent > 0; dvp_relation += 3; spd_relation += 3; dnvp_relation += 2; 

The Dutch Vrijzinnig-Democratische Bond and the Scandinavian liberal parties face the same problem we do: staying relevant as a small party squeezed between larger Socialist and Right-wing blocs. Their model of unification with other liberal forces, rather than staying alone, offers a blueprint we may find ourselves needing to follow.

@paneuropa
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; eu_progress += 1; pazifisten_strength += 3; nationalism -= 1*(1-dissent)

Count Coudenhove-Kalergi's vision of a united, peaceful Europe finds real apeal among our internationalist wing. Supporting the Pan-European movement costs us little and may, in time, yield much.

@league_of_nations
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; league_membership_support += 1; pazifisten_strength += 4; pazifisten_dissent -= 3 if pazifisten_dissent > 0; public_trust += 2; reparations_negotiation += 1

We have believed since our founding that Germany's rehabilitation runs through the League, not around it - full membership, not merely toleration from outside. Every step we take toward that goal is a step toward being treated as equals again, rather than a defeated power still serving out its sentence.

@america
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
go-to: america_democrats if america_contact = 0; america_republicans if america_contact = 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; america_contact += 1 if america_contact < 1

@america_democrats
on-arrival: west_relation += 1; democratization += 1

President Wilson's party shares much of our own political inheritance, but unfortunately his party finds itself out of power and increasingly isolationist since his stroke and the Senate's rejection of the League. We can still gain much from contacting them, though.

@america_republicans
on-arrival: west_relation += 1; nationalliberale_strength += 2; reparations_negotiation += 1

The Republican Party holds power in Washington, and its administrations control wether or not we must repay our war debts, loan capital, and pay reparations. They have little patience for the League or European entanglements, but their policies apeal to the more fiscally conservative in our party.

@return

We do not need the international contacts at the moment.
